double quotes appear in case['nodes']? Actually we wrote case['nodes'] with single quotes. So the entire Python source uses single quotes consistently. There is no double quotes in the Python source. Therefore we don't need to escape double quotes at all. But we must still escape backslashes? There are no backslashes except for the newline escape sequences we added. Those are \\n which is a valid escape in JSON. So we don't need to escape them further. However, to be safe, when writing JSON string, the backslash itself must be escaped if it's a literal backslash. But \\n is a JSON escape sequence, so we write the characters backslash and n. That's fine.\n\nTherefore our implementation string as written (with single quotes) is safe to put as JSON string value. We just need to ensure that the entire string is enclosed in double quotes and escaped properly for newlines (which we already have as \\n). So the final JSON is:\n\n{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = {n['id']: n for n in case['nodes']}\\n    threshold = case['utility_threshold']\\n    retained = set(nodes.keys())\\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes.values(), key=lambda n: (-n['depth'], n['id']))\\n    queue = [n['id'] for n in sorted_nodes]\\n    pending = set(queue)\\n    visit_order = []\\n    while queue:\\n        nid = queue.pop(0)\\n        pending.discard(nid)\\n        if nid not in retained:\\n            continue\\n        node = nodes[nid]\\n        visit_order.append(nid)\\n        children = [c for c in nodes.values() if c['parent'] == nid and c['id'] in retained]\\n        is_leaf = len(children) == 0\\n        if node['removable'] and node['utility'] <= threshold and is_leaf:\\n            retained.remove(nid)\\n            parent_id = node['parent']\\n            if parent_id is not None and parent_id in retained and parent_id not in pending:\\n                pending.add(parent_id)\\n                queue.append(parent_id)\\n    return {'retained_node_ids': sorted(list(retaine